/*
:name: concat_removed
:type: error
:error: `concat` was removed
:help: the argument order REVERSES
*/

// `concat(a, b, c)` was the positional bit-packing builtin, what SystemVerilog
// spells `{a, b, c}`. It was removed (docs/pyrope/21-deprecated.md): it read
// like `{a, b}` and was the only bit spelling in Pyrope that ran high-to-low,
// while `#[0]` is the low bit, a bit range is written low-to-high, and the
// string encoding puts the first characters in the low bits.
//
// The diagnostic is pinned HERE, not left to a generic "unknown call", because
// the migration is not a rename: `#[..]` puts entry 0 at bit 0, so the argument
// list REVERSES. Anything mechanical that keeps the old order miscompiles
// silently instead of failing, which is exactly what an error message is for.
comb concat_removed() -> (z:u12) {
  const a:u4 = 5
  const b:u8 = 1
  z = concat(a, b)   // the replacement is `(b, a)#[..]`
}
